{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "arkhe",
    "summary": "ARK identifier infrastructure — minter and resolver as separate services",
    "description": "Minting and resolution of ARK identifiers.\n\n**An ARK is never re-assigned (NR).** That one commitment shapes most of this API.\n\n* **A minted ARK cannot be withdrawn.** There is no delete; when an object is lost you\n  `tombstone` it (the description stays, only reachability goes).\n* **A resend does not mint again.** Send a `request_id` and the same value resent\n  returns the same ARK. Batches of tens of thousands are interrupted more often than\n  not, so an interrupted batch can simply be sent again.\n* **Naming a shoulder in a request does not widen anything.** Reach comes from the\n  credential's registration; omit it and the organisation's default is used.\n* **Child resources are not minted.** A deep reference such as\n  `ark:99999/x9tn1qkq2g7/page/3` is covered by suffix passthrough, so one record per\n  minting is enough.\n\n### Authentication\n\nPut a bearer token in via `Authorize`. Which credentials are accepted is set at start-up\nby `ARKHE_AUTH`: an API key, a token arkhe issued, or a JWT from an external\nauthorisation server (any combination).\n\n**Reading public information needs no authentication**, because a repository shows its\npublic records to anyone.\n",
    "license": {
      "name": "MIT",
      "identifier": "MIT"
    },
    "version": "0.2.0"
  },
  "paths": {
    "/oauth/token": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "oauth"
        ],
        "summary": "Issue an access token (client_credentials)",
        "description": "RFC 6749 §4.4 client_credentials.\n\nCredentials are accepted **in the body or by Basic authentication** (§2.3.1 recommends Basic and permits the body; client libraries in the wild use both).",
        "operationId": "token_oauth_token_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/x-www-form-urlencoded": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Body_token_oauth_token_post"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {}
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/api/mint": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "ark"
        ],
        "summary": "Mint",
        "description": "**Mint one new ARK.** Requires `ark:mint`.\n\nThe shoulder defaults to the organisation's own. Naming one in the request only asks\nwhether it lies inside the caller's registered reach — it never widens it.\n\n**Send a `request_id` and a resend will not mint again.** The same principal resending\nthe same `request_id` gets back the ARK minted the first time, so a lost response does\nnot leave a dead identifier behind. The status code says which happened:\n\n    201  minted\n    200  returned an earlier minting (a resend)\n\n**An ARK is never reissued**, so minting cannot be undone.",
        "operationId": "mint_api_mint_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MintIn"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ArkOut"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "200": {
            "description": "returned an earlier minting (a resend)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ArkOut"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "oauth2": [
              "ark:mint"
            ]
          },
          {
            "bearer": []
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/mint/bulk": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "ark"
        ],
        "summary": "Bulk Mint",
        "description": "**Mint in bulk.** Requires `ark:mint`. One request holds at most `ARKHE_BULK_LIMIT`\nrows (1000 by default).\n\n**One row out of reach and nothing is created.** Reach and shoulder are checked for\nevery row before any minting, so a half-minted batch cannot be left behind.\n\n**The answer keeps the order of the input**, because resent rows (a `request_id`\nalready seen) and new ones are mixed and the caller has to line them up. `created` and\n`replayed` carry the two counts; all resends answer 200, one new minting makes it 201.\n\nGive each row a `request_id` and **an interrupted batch can be sent again as it is** —\nrows already minted are skipped. **The same `request_id` twice inside one request still\nmints once**: it is one request, so it gets one number.",
        "operationId": "bulk_mint_api_mint_bulk_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BulkMintIn"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BulkMintOut"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "200": {
            "description": "every row was a resend",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BulkMintOut"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "oauth2": [
              "ark:mint"
            ]
          },
          {
            "bearer": []
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/register": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "ark"
        ],
        "summary": "Register",
        "description": "**Register a row for a qualified ARK** — an existing base name plus a qualifier.\n\nSuffix passthrough already covers a reference of any depth; this endpoint **overrides\nthat default at a single point**: \"this subtree lives in another store\", \"this\nderivative sits elsewhere\".\n\n**It requires `ark:mint`.** Nothing is minted, but a new resolvable identifier does\nappear, so it must not be handed to a principal that holds update rights alone.",
        "operationId": "register_api_register_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RegisterIn"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ArkOut"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "oauth2": [
              "ark:mint"
            ]
          },
          {
            "bearer": []
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/import": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "ark"
        ],
        "summary": "Import Ark",
        "description": "**Record an ARK that was minted elsewhere.** Requires `ark:import`.\n\nMinting does not let a caller choose the name; this does, and that single difference is\nwhy it has its own scope and its own checks. It exists so that **a name minted inside a\nclosed network can later be published under the same identifier** — without it, opening\nan embargoed object means issuing a different ARK, and every reference handed out while\nit was closed dies.\n\nThree things are checked, and none of them can be waived:\n\n* the shoulder is **delegated** — importing into a namespace this ledger mints in could\n  collide with its own minter, and a name minted elsewhere only exists because the\n  namespace was delegated in the first place;\n* the name falls **inside that shoulder**;\n* the **check digit verifies** — for a name that arrives from outside, that is the only\n  evidence there is that it was not mistyped.\n\nA name already in the ledger is refused rather than overwritten, exactly as minting is.",
        "operationId": "import_ark_api_import_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ImportIn"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ArkOut"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "oauth2": [
              "ark:import"
            ]
          },
          {
            "bearer": []
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/import/bulk": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "ark"
        ],
        "summary": "Bulk Import",
        "description": "**Import a whole delegated namespace at once.** Requires `ark:import`. One request holds\nat most `ARKHE_BULK_LIMIT` rows.\n\nThis is the shape the closed-network case actually needs: a delegate hands over the\nnames it minted, and they arrive together. Each row goes through exactly the same checks\nas a single import, and **one row that fails any of them means nothing is created** — a\nhalf-imported namespace is worse than none, because the names that did land cannot be\ntaken back.\n\nRows may span several shoulders, as long as every one of them is delegated and within\nthe caller's reach.",
        "operationId": "bulk_import_api_import_bulk_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BulkImportIn"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "201": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BulkImportOut"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "oauth2": [
              "ark:import"
            ]
          },
          {
            "bearer": []
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/update": {
      "put": {
        "tags": [
          "ark"
        ],
        "summary": "Update",
        "description": "Update an existing ARK. **The manager of the target's shoulder is checked.**",
        "operationId": "update_api_update_put",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/UpdateIn"
