    "/api/tombstone": {
      "put": {
        "tags": [
          "ark"
        ],
        "summary": "Tombstone",
        "description": "**Declare that the object is gone.** The ARK is not deleted.\n\nUnder NR (no re-assignment) an identifier cannot be removed; only reachability can be.\n**The identifier and its metadata stay**, and the resolver answers with the description.\n\n**Its scope is separate from `ark:update`.** A tombstone says \"this is gone\", not \"this\nis elsewhere\" — a different meaning with different consequences. It is hard to walk back\nand it is public, so it does not belong to routine writers such as an ingest batch.",
        "operationId": "tombstone_api_tombstone_put",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TombstoneIn"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ArkOut"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "oauth2": [
              "ark:tombstone"
            ]
          },
          {
            "bearer": []
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/hold": {
      "put": {
        "tags": [
          "ark"
        ],
        "summary": "Hold",
        "description": "**Stop redirecting, temporarily.** Resolution is not stopped — the description keeps\nbeing returned.\n\nFor when a delegate is down, a wrong target went out, or an object is moving: you have\nto stop quickly without killing the identifier. `404` would be a lie (the identifier\nexists) and `503` makes a permanent identifier look broken, so a hold answers **200 with\nthe description**, the same path a tombstone takes.\n\n**Its scope is separate from `ark:update`**, because stopping is a different decision\nfrom repointing and the reason is published. It is separate from a tombstone too: that\nis a permanent declaration, while this is **dated, and keeps the previous target**.",
        "operationId": "hold_api_hold_put",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HoldIn"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful Response",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ArkOut"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "oauth2": [
              "ark:hold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "bearer": []
          }
        ]
      }
    },
